Explore the GitHub Copilot Portal, especially through the GitHub web interface:
 
Step 1. Sign In and Enable Copilot https://github.com/copilot

1. Go to GitHub Copilot Portal. 

2. Sign in with your GitHub account.

3. Choose a plan (Free, Pro, or Pro+).

4. Enable Copilot and various AI Models from your settings. https://github.com/settings/copilot/features
 
Step 2: Import My sample repo: 

1. Import this repo into your github in case you do not have a repository
https://github.com/ShahabMohammed/AdvancedAutomated-AzureBugCretor
 
Step 3. Navigate to a Repository

1. Open any repository you own or have access to.

2, Click on a file (e.g., .js, .py, .md, etc.).
 
Step 4. Use Copilot Chat in the Portal

1. Click the Copilot icon (looks like a robot) in the top-right corner of the file view.

2. A chat panel opens on the left.
 
Step 5. Ask Your First Question

In the chat box at the bottom, try:

1. Explain this file

2. How can I improve this code?

3. Write a unit test for this class
 
Step 6. Continue the Conversation

Ask follow-ups like:

1. Tell me more

2. Can you optimize this code?

3. Add comments to this code

4. Enhance this file by adding exception handling, comments, XML comments to generate docfx.xml file
GitHub Copilot
AI that builds with you
 
